{"raw": {"https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29528": {"title": "Assistant Professor of Construction Management", "description": "FSU Job Site | Assistant Professor of Construction Management Skip to Main Content Fayetteville State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Titles Log In /Create Account Help Applicants FAQ'S Assistant Professor of Construction Management Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Please see Special Instructions for more details. The anticipated start date for the selected candidate is Spring 2027. Applications received by October 31, 2026, will receive priority consideration. Position Information Position Information Position Title: Assistant Professor of Construction Management Position Number: 000216 Working Title: Assistant Professor of Construction Management Full-time or Part-time: Full Time Time Limited Position: Yes Number of Vacancies: 1 Department: Dept of Accounting, Finance, HC Admin, & Info Systems (AFHAIS) Posting Number: 0401429 SHRA/EHRA: EHRA (Faculty) Job Category: Education and Instruction Hiring Range: Commensurate with Education and Experience Overall Position Competency: EHRA Faculty Primary Purpose of the Organization: Fayetteville State University is a constituent institution of the University of North Carolina System. AACSB International accredits the Broadwell College of Business and Economics ( BCBE ), providing an attractive and collegial academic environment with a strong focus on teaching, research, service, and community engagement. Primary Purpose of the Position: Broadwell College of Business and Economics at Fayetteville State University seeks to hire a non- tenure track, nine (9)-month faculty position at the rank of Assistant Professor for the Construction Project Management Program beginning Spring 2027. The selected candidate will exhibit a desire to teach at the undergraduate level but may also be required to teach graduate courses. The selected candidate will help develop and expand existing programs, concentrations, and minors. This position is funded by non-state funds and has been designated time limited. Continuation of this position is contingent upon the continuing availability of those funds. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements: A Ph.D. in Construction Management, Architectural Engineering, Civil Engineering, or a closely related discipline. All But Dissertation ( ABD ) candidates are welcome to apply. A minimum of one year of university-level teaching experience and/or industry-related experience. Record of relevant field/site work experience Knowledge skills and abilities: Skilled and dedicated teacher with student-oriented teaching philosophy who is willing to develop real world and community projects. Experience with construction technology tools, including BIM (Revit, Navisworks) Primavera P6 / MS Project Procore, Bluebeam, PlanGrid, AutoCAD. Preferred Qualifications: A Ph.D. in Construction Management, Architectural Engineering, Civil Engineering, or closely related discipline, at least two years of teaching and construction site experience, and relevant professional credentials such as: PMP (Project Management Professional)CM-Lean DBIA Certification OSHA 30 or Safety Certifications PE License (Civil/Structural) or RA (Registered Architect)Certified Professional Constructor ( CPC ) Special Instructions to Applicants: The anticipated start date for the selected candidate is Spring 2027. Applications received by October 31, 2026, will receive priority consideration. Notice to Applicants: Please make sure that the work history listed on your application is identical to the work history listed on your resume. The application must be filled out completely, Do Not Use the phrase \u201csee resume.\u201d Please list at least three (3) professional references to include a current supervisor. References will only be contact if you are selected for the position and with your permission. Closing Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Additional Information for Applicants: All new employees are required to have listed credentials/degrees verified prior to employment. Transcripts should be provided for all earned degrees and/or the degree which is being used to satisfy credential/qualification requirements. Transcript requests are the responsibility of the candidate. EEO Statement: This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable) and credit history check (if applicable). Fayetteville State University is committed to equality of educational opportunity and does not discriminate against applicants, students, or employees based on race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, political affiliation or sexual orientation. Moreover, Fayetteville State University values diversity and actively seeks to recruit talented students, faculty, and staff from diverse backgrounds. Veteran's Statement: Fayetteville State University is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Quick Link https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29201 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts and Official International Course-by-Course Evaluations Due Upon Hire) Optional Documents Other Document Other Documents Continued Other Documents Continued. MyBronco Portal Bookstore Library Jobs at FSU Contact Us News Events Directory Legal Fayetteville State University 1200 Murchison Road Fayetteville, NC 28301 Copyright \u00a9 May, 2018 Fayetteville State University. All Rights Reserved. Constituent Institution of The University of North Carolina. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29473": {"title": "Goodnight Distinguished Professor in Early Literacy", "description": "FSU Job Site | Goodnight Distinguished Professor in Early Literacy Skip to Main Content Fayetteville State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Titles Log In /Create Account Help Applicants FAQ'S Goodnight Distinguished Professor in Early Literacy Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Please see Special Instructions for more details. To make a nomination, provide a referral, or for additional information, please use the contact information below. While applications and nominations will be accepted until a successful candidate has been appointed, interested individuals are encouraged to submit their materials as soon as possible for full consideration as review of submitted materials will begin immediately. The ideal start date is summer 2027. To apply, please submit a resume and/or vita, and cover letter, to: FSUGoodnightProfessor@buffkinbaker.com. Martin Baker, Partner & Practice Leader, Buffkin / Baker 336.721.9100 Ken Carrick, Partner, Buffkin / Baker 980.296.5401 Janny DeLoache, Associate Partner, Buffkin / Baker 704.377.7828 Position Information Position Information Position Title: Goodnight Distinguished Professor in Early Literacy Position Number: 008053 Working Title: Goodnight Distinguished Professor in Early Literacy Full-time or Part-time: Full Time Time Limited Position: No Number of Vacancies: 1 Department: College of Education Posting Number: 0401431 SHRA/EHRA: EHRA (Faculty) Job Category: Education and Instruction Hiring Range: Commensurate with Education and Experience Overall Position Competency: EHRA Faculty Primary Purpose of the Organization: The College of Education at Fayetteville State University is committed to preparing highly qualified educators and leaders who are competent, committed, and caring. The College supports academic excellence through innovation in teaching, research, and service, and addresses the educational needs of diverse and underrepresented populations, especially in rural and underserved communities. Primary Purpose of the Position: The Goodnight Distinguished Professor in Early Literacy is an endowed faculty position established to support and enhance research, teaching, and service in the field of early literacy. This role is critical to driving impactful initiatives that improve literacy outcomes among young learners, particularly in rural and underserved communities. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements: An earned doctorate in Reading/Literacy Education or a closely related field. Tenured (or tenurable) at the Full Professor level. Nationally recognized record of scholarly excellence and research in early literacy. Demonstrated excellence in university-level teaching, mentoring, and leadership. Proven record of securing and managing external funding. Experience in building partnerships with schools, families, and communities. Knowledge skills and abilities: Expertise in the science of reading and early literacy theory and practice. Grant writing and project management skills. Effective teaching and mentoring skills. Culturally responsive pedagogy. Strong communication, collaboration, and leadership abilities. Preferred Qualifications: Special Instructions to Applicants: To make a nomination, provide a referral, or for additional information, please use the contact information below. While applications and nominations will be accepted until a successful candidate has been appointed, interested individuals are encouraged to submit their materials as soon as possible for full consideration as review of submitted materials will begin immediately. The ideal start date is summer 2027. To apply, please submit a resume and/or vita, and cover letter, to: FSUGoodnightProfessor@buffkinbaker.com. Martin Baker, Partner & Practice Leader, Buffkin / Baker 336.721.9100 Ken Carrick, Partner, Buffkin / Baker 980.296.5401 Janny DeLoache, Associate Partner, Buffkin / Baker 704.377.7828 Notice to Applicants: Please make sure that the work history listed on your application is identical to the work history listed on your resume. The application must be filled out completely, Do Not Use the phrase \u201csee resume.\u201d Please list at least three (3) professional references to include a current supervisor. References will only be contact if you are selected for the position and with your permission. Closing Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Additional Information for Applicants: All new employees are required to have listed credentials/degrees verified prior to employment. Transcripts should be provided for all earned degrees and/or the degree which is being used to satisfy credential/qualification requirements. Transcript requests are the responsibility of the candidate. EEO Statement: This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable) and credit history check (if applicable). Fayetteville State University is committed to equality of educational opportunity and does not discriminate against applicants, students, or employees based on race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, political affiliation or sexual orientation. Moreover, Fayetteville State University values diversity and actively seeks to recruit talented students, faculty, and staff from diverse backgrounds. Veteran's Statement: Fayetteville State University is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Quick Link https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29458 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Optional Documents MyBronco Portal Bookstore Library Jobs at FSU Contact Us News Events Directory Legal Fayetteville State University 1200 Murchison Road Fayetteville, NC 28301 Copyright \u00a9 May, 2018 Fayetteville State University. All Rights Reserved. Constituent Institution of The University of North Carolina. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}, "https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29312": {"title": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor for Allied Health (Respiratory Therapy)", "description": "FSU Job Site | Lecturer/Assistant Professor for Allied Health (Respiratory Therapy) Skip to Main Content Fayetteville State University Toggle navigation Home Search Jobs Search Titles Log In /Create Account Help Applicants FAQ'S Lecturer/Assistant Professor for Allied Health (Respiratory Therapy) Bookmark this Posting Print Preview | Apply for this Job Position Information Position Information Position Title: Lecturer/Assistant Professor for Allied Health (Respiratory Therapy) Position Number: 000854 Working Title: Lecturer/Assistant Professor for Allied Health (Respiratory Therapy) Full-time or Part-time: Full Time Time Limited Position: No Number of Vacancies: 1 Department: School of Nursing Posting Number: 0401428 SHRA/EHRA: EHRA (Faculty) Job Category: Education and Instruction Hiring Range: Commensurate with Education and Experience Overall Position Competency: Exempt Professional Staff (EPS) Primary Purpose of the Organization: The School of Nursing at Fayetteville State University is to educate culturally competent, ethical, and caring nurses for a global society. Nursing is a discipline that builds knowledge from nursing theory; the natural, social, and applied sciences; and the humanities. The School of Nursing is committed to educating graduates who will provide evidence-based and patient-centered care. The faculty value the systematic and purposeful application of the nursing process to promote the optimal health of clients throughout the life cycle and in a variety of settings. The School of Nursing strives to produce graduates who appreciate lifelong learning and are contributing to members to the profession of nursing, the community, and society. Primary Purpose of the Position: The School of Nursing invites applications for a faculty position to support the development, implementation, and continued growth of Allied Health academic programs, with an initial emphasis on the development and implementation of the University\u2019s Respiratory Therapy Program. The successful candidate will provide high quality instruction, contribute to curriculum and program development, participate in accreditation and assessment activities, advise and mentor students, and engage in university and professional service. As the University\u2019s Allied Health programs expand, the faculty member may support additional allied health disciplines consistent with their education, qualifications, and professional expertise. Appointment may be made at the rank of Lecturer or Assistant Professor based on the successful candidate\u2019s academic credentials, professional qualifications, experience, and university faculty appointment guidelines. Minimum Education and Experience Requirements: Master\u2019s degree in respiratory therapy or a closely related discipline from an accredited institution. Currently Registered Respiratory Therapist ( RRT ) credential. Eligibility for applicable state licensure. Demonstrated clinical experience in Respiratory Therapy. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to teach effectively in classroom, laboratory, simulation, and clinical settings. Candidates possessing a master\u2019s degree may be appointed at the rank of Lecturer . Candidates possessing an earned doctorate and meeting university faculty appointment standards may be appointed at the rank of Assistant Professor . Final rank will be determined based on academic credentials, professional experience, scholarship, and university appointment criteria. Knowledge skills and abilities: Knowledge of current Respiratory Therapy practice and education. Knowledge of accreditation standards applicable to Respiratory Therapy programs. Strong instructional and presentation skills. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Ability to establish collaborative relationships with students, faculty, clinical partners, and community stakeholders. Strong organizational and project management skills. Commitment to student success. Preferred Qualifications: Earned doctorate in Respiratory Therapy or closely related discipline. Previous college or university teaching experience. Experience developing or implementing Respiratory Therapy programs. Experience with accreditation and assessment. Curriculum development experience. Experience using simulation technologies. Evidence of scholarships, presentations, publications, or grant activity. Experience with online instruction and learning management systems. Special Instructions to Applicants: Notice to Applicants: Please make sure that the work history listed on your application is identical to the work history listed on your resume. The application must be filled out completely, Do Not Use the phrase \u201csee resume.\u201d Please list at least three (3) professional references to include a current supervisor. References will only be contact if you are selected for the position and with your permission. Closing Date: Open Until Filled: Yes Additional Information for Applicants: All new employees are required to have listed credentials/degrees verified prior to employment. Transcripts should be provided for all earned degrees and/or the degree which is being used to satisfy credential/qualification requirements. Transcript requests are the responsibility of the candidate. EEO Statement: This position is subject to the successful completion of an employment background check. An employment background check includes a criminal background check, employment verification, reference checks, license verification (if applicable) and credit history check (if applicable). Fayetteville State University is committed to equality of educational opportunity and does not discriminate against applicants, students, or employees based on race, religion, color, national origin, sex, age, disabling condition, political affiliation or sexual orientation. Moreover, Fayetteville State University values diversity and actively seeks to recruit talented students, faculty, and staff from diverse backgrounds. Veteran's Statement: Fayetteville State University is a VEVRAA Federal Contractor and seeks priority referrals of protected veterans for our openings. Quick Link https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29105 Supplemental Questions Required fields are indicated with an asterisk (*). Optional & Required Documents Required Documents Cover Letter Resume/Curriculum Vitae Unofficial Transcripts (Official Transcripts and Official International Course-by-Course Evaluations Due Upon Hire) Optional Documents Other Document Other Documents Continued Other Documents Continued. MyBronco Portal Bookstore Library Jobs at FSU Contact Us News Events Directory Legal Fayetteville State University 1200 Murchison Road Fayetteville, NC 28301 Copyright \u00a9 May, 2018 Fayetteville State University. All Rights Reserved. Constituent Institution of The University of North Carolina. To ensure the security of your data, you will be logged out due to inactivity in 3 minutes at . Any data not saved will be lost. Click 'OK' to keep your session active."}}, "rows": {"https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29528": {"school_id": 1941, "posting_url": "https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29528", "job_title_in_post": "Assistant Professor of Construction Management", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "Dept of Accounting, Finance, HC Admin, & Info Systems", "area_key_words": "Construction Management", "deadline_of_application": "October 31, 2026", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29473": {"school_id": 1941, "posting_url": "https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29473", "job_title_in_post": "Goodnight Distinguished Professor in Early Literacy", "position_type": "Full_Professor", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "College of Education", "area_key_words": "Early Literacy", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}, "https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29312": {"school_id": 1941, "posting_url": "https://jobs.uncfsu.edu/postings/29312", "job_title_in_post": "Lecturer/Assistant Professor for Allied Health (Respiratory Therapy)", "position_type": "Assistant_Professor; Lecturer", "job_term": "Full-time", "department_or_school": "School of Nursing", "area_key_words": "", "deadline_of_application": "", "position_start_date": ""}}, "school_id": 1941, "status": "complete", "updated_at": "2026-10-16T18:48:26+00:00", "completed_at": "2026-10-16T18:48:26+00:00", "last_error": ""}